# bcast_with_trigger.cm
#
# Demonstrates the collective-to-trigger chain built into the bcast branch.
#
# Phase 1: node 1 (index 0 of group 0) broadcasts 4 KiB to the six other
#          group members (2, 3, 6, 9, 12, 14).
#          When the *last* of those six sinks receives the last byte,
#          the internal BarrierTrigger fires and — via TriggerRelay —
#          activates trigger id 1.
#
# Phase 2: two P2P flows wait on trigger id 1 and launch simultaneously
#          once the broadcast is collectively complete:
#            flow 2 : root (1) -> master (0)
#            flow 3 : tail  (14) -> neighbour (15)
#
# Expected console output:
#   Trigger 100001 activated ... (six times, decrementing 5 -> 0)
#   Trigger 100001 fired, 2 targets          (no-op target + TriggerRelay)
#   Trigger 1 fired, 2 targets                (named trigger fires the two P2P flows)
Nodes 16
Grp 1 2 3 6 9 12 14
Connections 3
Triggers 1
0->0 id 1 start_bcast 0 size 4096 recv_done_trigger 1
1->0 id 2 trigger 1 size 4096
14->15 id 3 trigger 1 size 4096
trigger id 1 oneshot
